Ah, yes, the Grandeur of Omega.

Especially the IBM PC version.  The one that I dearchived, then proceded to
run.  The one that crashed and burned, locking out even a warm reset the first
time.  The one that got to "Your name, please?" the second time, then accessed
my hard disk for about 10 minutes before I turned it off.  The one that
actually managed, the third time, to activate a Hercules-compatible graphics
adapter I didn't even know I had, the third time I tried it.

Or perhaps you are referring to the net version, on which I came up with a
wonderful character, ran him up to seventh level, and then got the core dumped
out from under me, whenever I tried to restart his save file.

Ah, yes, that Grandeur.  Of course.

Let's all thank the development team, for keeping Nethack from becoming
another Omega.

                                     Thalen, the Omega-exhausted Mage

